 9 2 9 9\n9 9 2 9 9 2 9 9 2 9 9 2 9 9 2 9 9 2 9 9 2 9 9 2 9 9\n9 9 2 9 9 2 9 9 2 9 9 2 9 9 2 9 9 2 9 9 2 9 9 2 9 9\n9 9 2 9 9 2 9 9 2 9 9 2 9 9 2 9 9 2 9 9 2 9 9 2 9 9\n9 9 2 9 9 2 9 9 2 9 9 2 9 9 2 9 9 2 9 9 2 9 9 2 9 9\n2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 5 2 2 5 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2\n9 9 2 9 9 2 9 9 2 9 9 2 9 9 2 9 9 2 9 9 2 9 9 2 9 9\n9 9 2 9 9 2 9 9 2 9 9 2 9 9 2 9 9 2 9 9 2 9 9 2 9 9\n9 9 2 9 9 2 9 9 2 9 9 2 9 9 2 9 9 2 9 9 2 9 9 2 9 9\nWrong attempts used: 0/8. Demo requests used: 2/8.\nReply with exactly one action JSON on the last line.","reply":"```python\nfrom collections import Counter\n\ndef transform(grid):\n    h, w = len(grid), len(grid[0])\n    fill = Counter(x for row in grid for x in row).most_common(1)[0][0]\n\n    row_lines = [\n        r for r, row in enumerate(grid)\n        if Counter(row).most_common(1)[0][0] != fill\n    ]\n    col_lines = [\n        c for c in range(w)\n        if Counter(grid[r][c] for r in range(h)).most_common(1)[0][0] != fill\n    ]\n\n    out = []\n    for r1, r2 in zip(row_lines, row_lines[1:]):\n        row = []\n        for c1, c2 in zip(col_lines, col_lines[1:]):\n            corners = (\n                grid[r1][c1], grid[r1][c2],\n                grid[r2][c1], grid[r2][c2]\n            )\n            row.append(corners[0] if all(x == corners[0] for x in corners) else fill)\n        out.append(row)\n    return out\n```\n{\"action\":\"submit\"}","steps":[],"action":{"type":"submit","correct":false,"grid":[[2,9,5,9,9,9,3],[2,9,9,9,5,9,9]]}},{"step":35,"kind":"observation","phase":"act","t0":1792496480.7,"t1":1792496515.58,"alias":"task-a7c56f15","message":"Feedback since your last action:\nYour submission was INCORRECT. Wrong attempts so far: 1.\n\nSame instance. Task id: task-a7c56f15\nTest input (20x26):\n2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 5 2 2 5 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 3 2 2 3 2 2\n9 9 2 9 9 2 9 9 2 9 9 2 9 9 2 9 9 2 9 9 2 9 9 2 9 9\n9 9 2 9 9 2 9 9 2 9 9 2 9 9 2 9 9 2 9 9 2 9 9 2 9 9\n9 9 2 9 9 2 9 9 2 9 9 2 9 9 2 9 9 2 9 9 2 9 9 2 9 9\n9 9 2 9 9 2 